1.	Write a query to calculate the average age of employees in each department.
Query:
Select D.Name, avg(E.age) as AVG_AGE from Employees e Join Departments d
On e.department_id=d.id
Group by D.Name
;
Output:
+------------+---------+
| Name       | AVG_AGE |
+------------+---------+
| IT         | 37.5500 |
| HR         | 38.4000 |
| Finance    | 41.4500 |
| Marketing  | 41.4000 |
| Operations | 38.5500 |
+------------+---------+

2.	Write a query to find the department with the highest number of employees whose age is above 40.
Query:
With DEPARTEMENT_EMP_COUNT AS
(Select D.Name ,count(*) as Count from Employees e Join Departments d on d.id=e.department_id
Where Age>40
Group by D.Name
)
Select Name , Count from DEPARTEMENT_EMP_COUNT where Count=(Select Max(count) from DEPARTEMENT_EMP_COUNT);
Output:
+------------+-------+
| Name       | Count |
+------------+-------+
| Operations |   101 |
+------------+-------+

